1
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:04,690
Scoring back when I concede is my style of play!

2
00:00:04,690 --> 00:00:11,190
The final match of the Tokyo Regional Tournament, Toho Academy and Musashi Middle School, are battling neck and neck.

3
00:00:11,690 --> 00:00:16,000
Right after conceding 3 goals from Kojiro,

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,250
Musashi brought Misugi into the game earlier than planned.

5
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:24,920
Football is not a game played alone; it's a team game, Hyuga.

6
00:00:25,630 --> 00:00:29,800
As soon as he entered the game, he took the ball from Toho Academy

7
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:32,300
and is displaying magnificent play.

8
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:34,630
The gap is now down to one!

9
00:00:35,680 --> 00:00:38,430
I won't let you score another goal!

10
00:00:38,430 --> 00:00:42,900
It was Wakashimazu who stopped Misugi.

11
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:46,280
He prevented the goal with an incredible save.

12
00:00:46,280 --> 00:00:48,110
What are you, Wakashimazu?

13
00:00:48,110 --> 00:00:51,200
You're fast, your reflexes are solid, and your jumping ability...

14
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:53,610
It's impossible for me to score from long range.

15
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:56,360
The first half is over.

16
00:00:57,560 --> 00:01:00,900
It was so close. He almost scored.

17
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:05,870
Isn't Misugi magnificent? The game's atmosphere changed the moment he entered.

18
00:01:05,870 --> 00:01:11,250
He's cool, too. They're right to call him the Young Noble of the Field.

19
00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:17,590
Of course, Tsubasa is way cooler than him.

20
00:01:17,590 --> 00:01:19,740
Without a doubt.

21
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:23,350
He's very cool, but Misugi is also...

22
00:01:23,350 --> 00:01:27,990
Kumi, you don't even know why we're watching this match, do you?

23
00:01:27,990 --> 00:01:29,480
Of course I do!

24
00:01:29,480 --> 00:01:34,220
To find out who our opponent will be, and to record the matches to see their playing styles.

25
00:01:34,220 --> 00:01:35,360
As long as you know, it's fine.

26
00:01:35,360 --> 00:01:38,140
I have to go tell our guys!

27
00:01:43,030 --> 00:01:46,090
What? So Misugi entered the game in the first half, huh!

28
00:01:46,090 --> 00:01:46,770
Yes.

29
00:01:46,770 --> 00:01:47,580
Wow...

30
00:01:47,580 --> 00:01:50,280
Then who knows how the second half will go...

